133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (This report presents the results of a web vulnerability assessment performed on the Smit Cyber Security Demo Website using OWASP ZAP \(Zed Attack Proxy\) v2.17.0. The purpose of this assessment was to identify common web security weaknesses through passive scanning and to understand how professional vulnerability assessment tools are used during security testing.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (During the assessment, the website was accessed through the OWASP ZAP proxy, allowing HTTP and HTTPS traffic to be analyzed. The scan identified several security header-related findings, including the absence of Content Security Policy \(CSP\), X-Frame-Options, Strict-Transport-Security \(HSTS\), and X-Content-Type-Options headers. Informational findings related to cache behavior were also observed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (These findings are common in demonstration websites and provide valuable insight into web application security best practices. Appropriate mitigation recommendations have been included to explain how these issues can be addressed in production environments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (This project demonstrates the practical use of OWASP ZAP for identifying web application security issues and highlights the importance of secure HTTP response headers in improving overall web security.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
