298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (This project successfully demonstrated the process of performing a web application vulnerability assessment using OWASP ZAP. A demo website was developed, hosted locally, and assessed using passive scanning techniques. The assessment identified several low-risk security issues, primarily related to missing HTTP security headers and browser security best practices.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Although no critical or high-risk vulnerabilities were identified, the findings highlight the importance of implementing secure configurations to strengthen web application security. Appropriate recommendations have been provided to address each identified issue.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (This internship task provided valuable hands-on experience with industry-standard security tools, including OWASP ZAP, Nmap, Mozilla Firefox, and Visual Studio Code. It also improved practical knowledge of vulnerability assessment, security analysis, and professional report documentation.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
